(708472, 75100, 3765, '<td valign="top">This is an excellent idea. Looks very unnatural with the skew contents in the glasses. What would have made this photo superb is more emphasis om the rose. A lot lighter rose would have done the trick for me. 7</td>', 'This is an excellent idea. Looks very unnatural with the skew contents in the glasses. What would have made this photo superb is more emphasis om the rose. A lot lighter rose would have done the trick for me. 7', '2004-05-10 08:53:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(708477, 75555, 3765, '<td valign="top">This is one of the best landscape photo''s I have come across recently. The composition is good. Light is good. Use of foreground excellent. I hope you do very well in this challenge. 10</td>', 'This is one of the best landscape photo''s I have come across recently. The composition is good. Light is good. Use of foreground excellent. I hope you do very well in this challenge. 10', '2004-05-10 09:01:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(708480, 74645, 3765, '<td valign="top">Brilliant!. The only negative thing I can say is that the information-signs are a bit washed out. Btw, did you use maximum aperture because I can see some blue lines next to the highlights that look like some kind of abberation. Closing the aperture somewhat can solve this problem. Very nice shot. 9</td>', 'Brilliant!. The only negative thing I can say is that the information-signs are a bit washed out. Btw, did you use maximum aperture because I can see some blue lines next to the highlights that look like some kind of abberation. Closing the aperture somewhat can solve this problem. Very nice shot. 9', '2004-05-10 09:05:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(708485, 75208, 3765, '<td valign="top">Good composition and nice use of colours. Strawberry can be a bit lighter. 8 from me although the combination has put my tastebuds off food for the day.</td>', 'Good composition and nice use of colours. Strawberry can be a bit lighter. 8 from me although the combination has put my tastebuds off food for the day.', '2004-05-10 09:09:18.000000', NULL, 1),
