(944096, 75490, 26238, '<td valign="top">beautiful baby with the most beautiful eyes. i love everything about it. the color, the expression, the lighting. good job.</td>', 'beautiful baby with the most beautiful eyes. i love everything about it. the color, the expression, the lighting. good job.', '2004-10-06 00:44:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(993765, 75573, 23394, '<td valign="top">christina, <i>this</i> is a stunning image!  the colors are simply incredible.  it''s not often that nature presents us these opportunities; i''m glad you were there to take advantage of it.<br/> <br/>from a composition standpoint, it doesn''t appear that the near sky has too much to offer.  with that in mind, in situations like this, you might want to angle for more foreground and less sky; this would also keep the horizon from splitting the image in the middle.  <br/> <br/>another thing to keep in mind to really nail these shots are your settings.  i''m not sure of the range available on the camera you shot this with, but with your current camera, i can only begin to imagine how this would have turned out with aperature at F10 and a shutter near 100.<br/> <br/>(just for grins, another shot that might have been fun would be to have moved to the left and turned the camera sideways for a portrait shot that really focused on the rope and the boat.)<br/> <br/>thanks again for sharing a beautiful image.  i''m glad it did so well for you.</td>', 'christina, this is a stunning image!  the colors are simply incredible.  it''s not often that nature presents us these opportunities; i''m glad you were there to take advantage of it. from a composition standpoint, it doesn''t appear that the near sky has too much to offer.  with that in mind, in situations like this, you might want to angle for more foreground and less sky; this would also keep the horizon from splitting the image in the middle.   another thing to keep in mind to really nail these shots are your settings.  i''m not sure of the range available on the camera you shot this with, but with your current camera, i can only begin to imagine how this would have turned out with aperature at F10 and a shutter near 100. (just for grins, another shot that might have been fun would be to have moved to the left and turned the camera sideways for a portrait shot that really focused on the rope and the boat.) thanks again for sharing a beautiful image.  i''m glad it did so well for you.', '2004-11-05 17:24:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1040078, 75541, 30113, '<td valign="top">Gread Photo ,just like all youer other Pic.</td>', 'Gread Photo ,just like all youer other Pic.', '2004-12-01 03:18:03.000000', NULL, 0);
